envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-export-schema-failure_mode
type: schema
id: failure_mode
context: >-
  cortex/schemas — sovereign local copy. cortex/self-heal/index.js + failure-mode-forensics.js are
  the real writers. Origin: lib/node-schemas/schema.failure_mode.
intent: null
summary: null
system: cortex
tags: []
exported_at: 1789253941194
source: nexus.lib.node-export
payload:
  status: REAL
  source: >-
    cortex/self-heal/index.js's real _enterFailureMode(gapType, gapUuid, existing) ("Level 4 —
    failure mode, human action item") writes real jaaDB rows to a real `failure_modes` table, read
    back via cortex/boot.js's real GET /api/failure-modes (jaaDB.tail('failure_modes', 20)).
    correction_2026-09-12 — James: "each system needs .failure_mode nodes that use the intelligence
    system to map the events leading up to a failure mode... delta and sigmas for tension and
    friction score." The causal context (root/conditions/siblingDanglingHooks) was already being
    gathered by the same file's own _gatherFailureContext() — real, working, via lib/gap-field.js's
    explainWhy() -> lib/diagnostic-causal.js's explainFinding() -> intelligence/relational-field —
    but only ever flattened into a RAID contract's free-text content, never persisted as structured
    data on the failure_mode record itself. cortex/self-heal/failure-mode-forensics.js now does
    that: an async, best-effort UPDATE onto the same row once real context resolves (never delays or
    risks the original synchronous §0.3 write above), adding the fields below.
  fields:
    uuid:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real failure-mode entry id
    faultClass:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real fault classification — the gapType that escalated to this level
    gapUuid:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real id of the .gap that escalated into this failure mode
    friction:
      type: number
      required: false
      description: real friction score carried over from the escalating gap, defaults to 1.0
    enteredAt:
      type: number
      required: true
      description: real timestamp this failure mode was entered
    source:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real originating module — cortex/self-heal/index.js's own MODULE_ID
    root:
      type: any
      required: false
      description: >-
        correction_2026-09-12: real root-cause object from lib/diagnostic-causal.js's
        explainFinding(), when the causal field traced one — added by failure-mode-forensics.js's
        async enrichment, absent if the causal field had none
    conditions:
      type: array
      required: false
      description: >-
        correction_2026-09-12: real, ordered list of precursor conditions/events from the same
        causal trace — the actual "events leading up to it," not a guess
    siblingDanglingHooks:
      type: array
      required: false
      description: >-
        correction_2026-09-12: real dangling hooks found on the same system at the time of failure,
        may or may not be related — carried over from _gatherFailureContext() unchanged
    sigmaBefore:
      type: number
      required: false
      description: >-
        correction_2026-09-12: real average sigma_records reading in the window before this failure,
        when any were recorded — see failure-mode-forensics.js computeSigmaDelta()
    sigmaAtEntry:
      type: number
      required: false
      description: >-
        correction_2026-09-12: real average sigma_records reading in the window immediately before
        entry, closest to the actual failure
    sigmaDelta:
      type: number
      required: false
      description: >-
        correction_2026-09-12: real sigmaAtEntry - sigmaBefore — a rising delta means system-wide
        tension was climbing into this failure, not assumed causal, just observed
    debugMacroUuid:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: >-
        correction_2026-09-12: real id of the .debug_macro generated to reproduce this failure, when
        conditions were available to build one
    contextGatherError:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: >-
        correction_2026-09-12: honest error message if context-gathering itself failed — never
        silently omitted
    enrichedAt:
      type: number
      required: false
      description: >-
        correction_2026-09-12: real timestamp the async enrichment update landed, distinct from
        enteredAt
    compound:
      type: any
      required: false
      description: >-
        correction_2026-09-28 (staging-self-heal phasemap C1): chain-scoped compound reading from
        intelligence/causal/compound.js, stored under its OWN key, never merged into the system-wide
        sigmaBefore/sigmaAtEntry/sigmaDelta above (I10). Shape: {status: analyzed|unavailable, reason,
        class: ripple|wave|tidal|null, factors, sigmaProgression, deltaProgression, peakSigma, rootUuid,
        anchor: {ledgerSystem, entryUuid}}. status unavailable (no anchor, unknown system, entry not in that
        system graph, orchestrator unreachable) carries a reason and class null — never a ripple (I8/I9).
        A ripple has no CausalRecord by design: class ripple with factors/progressions null. rootUuid is
        the chain TRUE ROOT analyzeChain walked to, which may differ from anchor.entryUuid.
